            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "extrañar — \"to miss (someone); to find strange\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Te extraño mucho. I miss you a lot."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "To miss is the Latin American sense; in Spain people mostly say echar de menos. Me extraña — I find it strange."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "extrañar is inherited from Late Latin extrāneāre, built on extrāneus \"external, foreign, strange\" (EtymDB); English strange comes from the same adjective through French."
            }
          ]
        },
